# Recorded:     2026-08-21 at commit b2283b0
# Reason:       TODO #34: fixed-density is now min(rho,1)*target_density in ALL FOUR places that compute it, not just Grid::clampFixedDensity. #3 (2026-08-17) changed the solver field but left computeOverflow, pl_algo density_bin.hpp and test/density_bin_model.cpp on the old min(rho,td) cap. computeOverflow is the CONVERGENCE SIGNAL (Output.cpp smoothed call + Phase2 transition), so sw_only was optimizing one density map and deciding when to stop from another on every td<1 design. Effect: mgc_fft_a (td=0.50) HPWL -1.05%, 632->611 iters; mgc_pci_bridge32_b (td=0.14) HPWL -20.67%, 713->651 iters. mms_adaptec1 (td=1.0) BIT-IDENTICAL, as required -- the two formulas are algebraically equal at td=1, which is the control proving only the intended thing changed.
#
# DO NOT refresh this file to make a failing test pass. Read the diff first: the
# body below is the full per-iteration trajectory, so the row where it starts to
# differ tells you what changed and when. See test/regress/README.md.
